<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SAVINGS BANKS' Q1 OPERATING PROFITS ROSE.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SAVINGS BANKS' Q1 OPERATING PROFITS ROSE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The savings banks' total operating profit in the first quarter rose to 72 million markka from 60 million in the year-ago period, the savings banks' association said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The savings banking group profit was made up of Aktia's 15 million markka operating profit and the other savings banks' 56 million markka operating profit,&quot; it said, adding that all savings banks made profits in the first quarter.  </p>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997-</p>
<p>				    (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit after credit losses	  72 vs 60</p>
<p> Credit losses					 17 vs 19</p>
<p> Net income from financial operations	 205 vs 193</p>
<p> Other income					  82 vs 77</p>
<p> Capital adequacy, percent		     14.4 vs 12.9</p>
<p> Non-performing credit			    413 vs 545</p>
<p> Personnel expenses				  90 vs 83</p>
<p> Other expenses					95 vs 96</p>
<p> Depreciation					   8 vs 9</p>
<p> Total expenses				     193 vs 188</p>
<p> Write-downs					    4 vs 4</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0235, news@reuters.fi</p>
